glm5next MTP draft: cache-only catch-up graph. Deployed 2026-09-19. Draft-side only; target arithmetic untouched.
GGML_GLM5N_MTP_KV_ONLY=1, default off. Only models/glm5next.cpp changes over the deployed libllama
(parent e77a573df69456745857677e71e4e9cc876b8294384fa7798629f3ebe7c3306a, result 65670d4a19178bbdffcfbc79ee953e5319083875309ed52aa4de214393e20ce3).

After every verify batch the MTP driver refreshes the draft layer's KV cache with a batch that requests NO outputs, yet the graph
still built the query projection, attention, MoE and LM head. With zero outputs the graph now stops after the KV latent is
normalised and stored (15 nodes instead of 89).

Evidence (engineering/2026-09-20/archive/sr950-strategy/codex-bench-0919/MTP-KV-RESULT.md): standalone, real 9.26 GB MTP sidecar, four NUMA
devices, 170 records / 28,400,396 bytes equal (cache tensors, logits, hidden rows) at 1 and 15 workers. Same loaded model, ABBA then
BAAB, eight cached Codex-in-Paseo runs, identical text and counters: 15.43 -> 15.82 tok/s (+2.5%). Draft work 21.3 -> 18.2 ms per
cycle. A separate-stream sequence-copy crash in the REFERENCE runtime is preserved in that directory and is not fixed.

